WEBVTT

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.080
Gundam...

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.710
That thing is built with psycho-frame throughout the body?

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:54.650
No doubt about it. The unidentified single-horned suit transformed...

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.090
...no, morphed!

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:57.720
That's a Gundam!

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.030
Gundam...

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.760
It really... It really is a Gundam.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.040
Gundam?

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.770
The first mobile suit developed by the Federation.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.560
Zeon called it the White Devil.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:10.270
Bridge!

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:15.320
The machine that's engaging the Sleeves' quad-wing definitely looks like a Gundam type!

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.670
Seriously, a Gundam?!

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.530
Gundam...

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.930
Gundam... is the enemy!

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:15.800
Attention unidentified machine, reply if you can hear me!

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:20.430
Please identify your affiliation and your combat objective.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.430
I repeat...

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.370
A wretched fiasco, Suberoa Zinnerman.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:30.750
You were neither able to obtain Laplace's Box, nor rescue the princess.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.830
None of these developments could have been foreseen.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:37.800
For now, we have no choice but to wait to hear from the princess.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.860
Meaning you want us to sit around and do nothing?!

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.420
Lieutenant Angelo...

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:46.030
I hear the enemy that drove off Marida was a Gundam.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.680
Intriguing.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.040
I might just need to go out there myself.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.210
Have the Garencieres find out the Federation ship's next move.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:54.520
Yes sir.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.650
I will rectify this fiasco even if it costs me my life.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.430
Don't let past mistakes weigh you down.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:04.220
Just learn from them and move on.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.390
That's the privilege of being an adult.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.180
<b>The Second Coming of Char</b>

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.360
Mom...

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.370
Riddhe...

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.270
I want you to know you were lucky.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.480
Surviving doesn't mean you're a coward.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.940
Any more than dying means you were brave.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:05.240
The only thing that separates the two is luck.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.320
Yes, Commander Norm.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.580
Attention approaching vessel, you are ordered to halt immediately.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:15.040
This is the Nahel Argama of the Federation Space Forces, Londo Bell.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:18.540
Your vessel has crossed our defensive perimeter.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.040
Damned terrorists!

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.070
Wait.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:27.240
It's trash?!

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.260
It appears to be a wrecked Salamis class.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.310
Its reserve power supply is still alive.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.140
Seems the thermal sensors misidentified it.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.270
Cancel the alert. Return to your stations.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.580
And recall the mobile suits.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:39.910
Are you sure?

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:41.280
Is there a problem?

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:43.690
It was just misidentified debris?

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:47.090
Yep. We're lucky it wasn't an enemy out there.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.370
Enemies will appear though.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:54.500
They probably think that we recovered Laplace's Box.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:59.100
And as long as that quad-wing mobile suit is still kicking...

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:02.360
So this is no time to wait for reinforcements.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.550
That's right.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:05.130
Have you gotten it open yet?

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:05.880
Well...

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:10.300
I didn't expect the system to be so resistant to outside interference.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:14.520
Meaning you weren't told anything outside of your specific department?

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.020
Yes.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:19.440
Once the UC Project was placed under the Vist Foundation's jurisdiction

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.320
the entire picture was never...

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.010
Hey! Enough chatter! Shut your mouth!

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:26.820
This line is closed.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:31.870
What's the UC Project?

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:36.550
ECOAS can't investigate this by ourselves.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:40.460
If we did, our guest from Anaheim would meddle in it as if he were the top brass.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:49.470
The UC Project is a top secret program, part of the E.F.S.F. Reorganization Plan.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.780
This Unicorn is the flagship.

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:57.480
The entire body uses psycho-frame technology, which supplements the psycommu,

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.400
transmitting the pilot's psycho-waves directly to the drive system.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:05.800
Which means the pilot can control it just by thinking.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:09.490
But the pilot's body can't really take that, right?

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.220
No.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:15.620
But the NT-D is supposed to have a time limit of only 5 minutes once activated.

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.700
This "NT-D" is...

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.340
Commander Daguza!

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:25.360
I told you that I should be present when you're interrogating rescued staff!

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:26.610
Captain Otto.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:30.450
It would be wise for us to leave this sector with a single ship right now.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:36.430
Chances are the recovered Gundam type has something to do with Laplace's Box!

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:39.620
Please set a course for Luna II as soon as possible.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:40.810
That may be, but...

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:42.750
I agree, Captain!

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.880
But we shouldn't go to Luna II.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:49.010
We should head for our Anaheim Electronics headquarters,

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.280
at Von Braun on the moon.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:54.760
Attention. Entering second deployment.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.220
Watch out for sections under security lockdown.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:58.190
Wait here for now.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:00.360
Second patrol is now on duty.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.820
You still don't know who was piloting that Gundam?

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:05.620
We don't. Apparently the cockpit hatch hasn't opened yet.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:06.900
It's you.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.230
Are you all right?

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.520
I'm the pilot who rescued you guys.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:13.910
My name's Riddhe Marcenas.

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.470
I'm Audrey Burne.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:18.470
Want to go check it out?

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:20.470
That Gundam.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:21.500
It's on your mind, isn't it?

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.820
Ensign Riddhe...

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.690
We'll be fine, Ensign Mihiro.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.280
I know a secret spot where we can sneak a look.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.480
That's not what I meant.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.250
Yeah! Let's go!

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:36.630
This Nahel Argama was the mothership of the Gundam Team in the first Neo Zeon War!

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:39.850
This must be fate for it to carry the new Gundam now!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.180
Yeah.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.350
Let's go, Micott. You're coming too!

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:50.010
I'm going too.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:55.390
If it hadn't been for that Gundam, we would've all been annihilated.

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.560
I want to know who was piloting it, too.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:05.650
Unlike Luna II, which is on the far side of the Earth, the Moon is right next to us.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.380
The enemy will expect us to head for the moon.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.780
We should set a course for Luna II, even if it's a detour.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:16.380
We can get to the moon with the resources we have left, can't we?

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:19.540
I think the Commander is just impatient.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.760
Traveling with no hope of reinforcements, I'll be even less patient.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:27.770
We're in this situation because of civilians who've put pressure on the military chain of command.

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:31.000
The duty of a soldier is to carry out orders.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.220
Don't blame us for your failure.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:33.010
Cut the transmission.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:34.220
Now!

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:38.220
I know ECOAS can do as they please during an operation

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:40.780
but I wish they'd get off our backs while we're giving them a ride.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:43.730
That goes for that high maintenance executive from Anaheim, too.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.500
No use complaining if he can't hear you.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:52.880
That wreckage we encountered has decelerated.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.780
Now traveling at relative velocity zero.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:58.030
Haunted by ghosts of the One Year War, eh?

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:00.680
Have the mobile suits eliminate it.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:02.630
They can push aside something that size, no problem.

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.910
But they've already returned.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.080
What?

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.270
Those were your orders, sir.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.270
Do you want to order them to launch again?

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:14.940
Just blast it with the main guns!

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:25.580
Got it.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.210
Enemy's position confirmed.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.020
Transmit the coordinates to the Rewloola.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.960
Then let's wait and see what they do.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.420
That's a Gundam?

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:41.670
That's what they say, but it looks completely different.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:44.410
I feel like I've seen you somewhere before.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:50.600
I know!

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:56.440
Natsume Swanson, the actress! Do people tell you that you look like her?

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:00.320
I don't know much about the entertainment world, so...

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:01.930
Okay.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:03.310
Hey, Mr. Ensign!

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.330
The hatch is opening!

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.040
Banagher?! Why're you—?!

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:29.960
He doesn't look like a pilot!

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:38.760
Banagher!

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:39.400
Doctor!

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:43.480
Banagher...

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:44.820
Hey, are you okay?

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:48.750
Audrey...

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:53.790
Banagher, can you hear me?

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.860
If you can hear me, squeeze my hand, all right?

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:58.530
Bridge, this is Mihiro.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.740
The boy's regained consciousness.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:02.470
Commander Daguza?!

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:03.780
I'd like to ask him some questions.

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:05.800
The rest of you, leave. Now.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:07.160
Yes, sir, but...

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:09.200
At least let me finish giving him his treatment.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:12.870
He still has no idea where he is.

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:14.960
You understand that he's injured, don't you?

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:21.550
I understand this boy hijacked a military mobile suit and interfered in combat.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:24.950
It is a violation severe enough to warrant capital punishment.

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:26.870
Capital punishment...

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:30.370
He saved us, didn't he?

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.100
But with a stolen machine.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:35.880
We're ready to launch.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:39.340
Sit here and observe, Captain.

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:43.930
This has got to be related to Laplace's Box, huh?

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:47.740
If this secret is so important that they sent ECOAS to recover it...

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.640
There's a limit to how much the Federation can mobilize in secrecy.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:56.000
Right now, they're likely in discussions about how to handle it.

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:59.110
Talks between everyone responsible who doesn't want the responsibility.

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:00.810
I hope you're right.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:03.630
There's no sign of reinforcements, is there? I assure you.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.640
The Captain is going out today.

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.810
There won't be any work for us.

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:23.760
Can't say I'm convinced by that story.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:28.160
You say Cardeas Vist just handed that thing over to a random boy like you?

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:31.560
And did he say anything else?

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:35.790
Like I said, he told me to take the mobile suit and use it to protect everyone.

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:37.310
That's all.

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:42.780
Would you believe me if I told you he was my father?

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:53.620
All units, scramble!

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.010
Turn about, full speed!

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:56.650
Quick! Get me a damage report!

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:57.710
Anti-air surveillance!

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:59.380
No sign of enemies nearby!

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.650
Look harder!

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:12.450
We were set up.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:15.790
This is because you took too long to make a decision!

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:15.790
Cut it!

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:19.210
Intense heat sources approaching at high speed.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:22.210
There are four total. They're coming in from directly above!

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:23.070
What?! Missiles?!

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.820
Not likely. Their movement is...

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:27.880
I'd say mobile suits, but...

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:30.850
It's going through the debris.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:33.930
Unbelievable!

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.830
The lead machine is approaching at

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.920
three times the speed of the others!

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:49.110
Let's see... Let's test the performance of your new Gundam.

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:52.390
All hands, prepare for anti-air combat!

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:54.760
Are these the same guys that attacked the colony?!

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:56.620
I can't take this anymore!

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:57.270
Micott!

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:58.870
We've got to look for normal suits.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:00.920
This ship could get a hole blasted through it any minute now!

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:02.710
Everyone! Put these on!

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:05.570
What happened to the other girl?

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:09.680
Interceptor system set to automatic fire!

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:11.970
Remaining enemy mobile suits are still in flight!

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:13.240
You. Where do you think you're going?

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:16.080
Put on a normal suit and get to shelter!

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.060
Anti-air defenses, what are you doing?

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:40.580
I can't get a lock on the—

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:42.520
Just start firing!

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:49.010
Romeo 008 ready to launch!

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:50.970
Pilot to the mobile suit deck immediately!

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:54.620
Here you go.

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.330
Thanks!

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:00.480
You're awake now.

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:02.750
It might save my life.

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:04.460
This is my good luck charm.

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:05.940
You stay here and rest up.

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:07.840
There's nothing for you to do.

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:11.740
We'll protect our own ship this time!

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:15.120
A kid like that in control of a Gundam...

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:17.290
Banagher!

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:19.910
Audrey.

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:21.960
Banagher, listen to me...

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:26.940
That machine is registered to your biometric data

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.570
which means it can't operate without you.

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:31.340
That's what I was told, but...

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:33.820
How do you know that?

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:35.430
Escape with me.

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:39.990
Rear main gun is damaged!

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:42.140
Severe damage reported on port side bulkhead seven.

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:44.560
Ensign Mihiro to the bridge, now!

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:47.150
Damn these amateurs!

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:50.440
As long as they think we have the Box

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:55.050
they'll try to neutralize our ship without hitting the engines.

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:58.280
It's hard to believe that a single mobile suit could...

00:15:58.870 --> 00:15:59.870
That says...

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:02.160
This ship is carrying something

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:05.100
almost as important to them as the Box.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.750
If we go now, we can get away.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:09.070
We can go back to Industrial 7.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:13.300
You sneak onto a cargo ship, get to another Side, then go into hiding.

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:18.070
And I'll figure out some way to dispose of that machine.

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:19.280
Audrey...?

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:20.470
If we don't...

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.680
That thing is just too dangerous.

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:25.060
I can't let anyone get their hands on it.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:27.040
Wait a minute...

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:29.540
I'll explain more later.

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.860
If you won't tell me anything, how can you expect me to agree with you?

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:36.570
Don't try to sway me by talking like that. It's not fair.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:39.870
What do you want to do?

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:44.040
Don't tell me what you should do. Tell me what you want.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:47.000
Tell me what you truly want to do.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.090
And then I...

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:55.820
What are you—?!

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:58.070
You know why I'm here?

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:03.640
Audrey!

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:06.060
Course is set!

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:09.150
Catapult hatches one through four, open!

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:11.940
Mobile suit corps, get into position to launch.

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:20.950
Are you getting scared, little man?

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:24.040
Nah, but I heard a squeak in your voice just now, Lieutenant Homare.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:26.750
There you go trying to start something.

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:30.230
Norm Basilicock.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:31.940
Romeo 001, launch!

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:37.300
Galom Gorga. Juliet 002 launch!

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:40.470
Riddhe Marcenas.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:42.180
Romeo 008. Here I go!

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:56.170
Severe damage reported on port side catapult deck.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:57.380
Lieutenant Homare!

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.280
Hurry up with the damage report!

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:01.140
Get out of here and go to the moon right now!

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:03.600
Mr. Alberto, it's dangerous for you to be in here!

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.430
That's the Sinanju! The Red Comet!

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:08.430
There's no way you can defeat it.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:14.800
Two years ago, our experimental mobile suit MSN-06S was stolen by Neo Zeon

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:20.590
while it was being transferred from the lunar city Granada to a testing ground at Von Braun.

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:25.330
The Federation Forces that were sent to pursue it were wiped out instead.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.980
The primary culprit was...

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:32.150
Full Frontal,

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:36.550
the man they call the Second Coming of Char Aznable, the Red Comet.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:43.410
I've heard something like that.

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:47.720
The "Ghost of Char", who destroyed two Clop-class ships with a single mobile suit.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:53.250
But Char went missing during the Second Neo Zeon War.

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:58.280
Anyway, we can't expect to beat him with ordinary mobile suits.

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:02.720
The Unicorn was made using data collected with the Sinanju.

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:04.600
We've got to get out of here now.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:09.080
Running away will leave us open to attack from behind!

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:11.580
Transfer the verification data to each section of the ship!

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:13.600
The enemy is not actually a ghost!

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:15.610
Send it to the mobile suit corps, too!

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:17.020
You're an idiot without a clue.

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:18.690
And you're the last person I wanna hear that from!

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:33.810
There it is!

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:43.890
Don't rush in, Ensign Riddhe. Stay in formation.

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:48.280
Galom. Below you!

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:55.330
That can't be the real Char?!

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:57.330
Lieutenant Angelo...

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:00.070
There are multiple enemies. We should at least provide some cover.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:03.780
No, we need only stand by, Ensign Sergi.

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:05.970
We'd only get in the Captain's way.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:17.080
At this rate, everyone will...

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:18.920
Attention, all attacking machines, do you read me?

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:21.630
Cease fire immediately.

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:24.700
We are holding Mineva Zabi captive aboard this ship.

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:26.890
I repeat...

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:30.850
We are holding the Zabi heir, Mineva Lao Zabi, captive aboard this ship.

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:35.520
If you do not cease your attacks immediately, we cannot guarantee her safety.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:38.490
That girl is the Princess of Zeon?

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:42.780
We are prepared to begin negotiations, and await your wise response.

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:46.820
I've verified the image.

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:50.450
I am Captain Full Frontal of Neo Zeon.

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:52.120
Let's hear your demands.

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:54.290
That's Char's voice...

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:57.290
This is Commander Daguza Mackle

00:20:57.290 --> 00:21:00.460
of the Earth Federation Space Force Special Operations Group, ECOAS.

00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:04.360
We're requesting you cease all attacks and withdraw immediately.

00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:08.680
If you do, we will guarantee the safety of Mineva Zabi.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:11.370
So we can't have her back?

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:18.350
It's negotiable, but only after our ship has reached a safe location.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.610
Then you're not holding her captive, you're holding her hostage.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:25.700
And we have no evidence that you have the real Princess Mineva.

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:31.390
Rather timid, for a man called the Second Coming of the Red Comet.

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:35.160
From your point of view, we're merely terrorists.

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.420
Any group unrecognized as military and

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:41.000
unprotected by international law needs to be cautious.

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:43.500
We have the highest regard for human rights.

00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:48.380
That's quite a statement coming from those who send special forces into civilian colonies.

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:51.720
And now you're using hostages as shields.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:55.390
Now it's our turn to make some demands.

00:21:56.850 --> 00:21:59.520
I request you hand over the materials you collected from Industrial 7

00:21:59.860 --> 00:22:04.440
and all data pertaining to Laplace's Box.

00:22:06.610 --> 00:22:07.610
And in exchange?

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:10.160
We'll guarantee your safe passage.

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:11.820
Unless you object to that arrangement.

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:14.330
I have no objection, but we are unable to comply.

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:17.370
We don't have anything related to Laplace's Box.

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:21.830
Didn't you recover a Gundam type mobile suit?

00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:23.630
That's the property of the Federation Forces.

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:25.460
It has nothing to do with the Box.

00:22:25.960 --> 00:22:29.130
If you can't accept our demands, we'll be forced to destroy your vessel.

00:22:29.970 --> 00:22:31.760
You would ignore the life of our captive?

00:22:32.350 --> 00:22:35.720
We can't conduct negotiations based on an uncertain factor.

00:22:37.980 --> 00:22:39.140
I'll give you three minutes.

00:22:39.770 --> 00:22:41.350
I hope you'll have come to a wise decision.

00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:53.070
He's bluffing. He wouldn't forsake the guiding star of the Zeon remnants.

00:22:53.410 --> 00:22:54.580
I don't know about that...

00:22:56.790 --> 00:23:01.620
If Full Frontal is really Char Aznable

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:03.380
he'd be the son of Zeon Deikun.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:07.190
There's no reason an enemy of the Zabi family would care about their descendants.

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:11.900
The way you say that makes me believe you're the real Mineva Zabi.

00:23:20.850 --> 00:23:24.770
And I'm certain a good number of those Sleeves soldiers believe in the Zabi family.

00:23:25.110 --> 00:23:28.530
If you truly believe that, then continue these useless negotiations.

00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:32.280
But the soldiers of Zeon don't play as nicely as you do.

00:23:32.990 --> 00:23:38.660
If you were a Zeon soldier, you'd be figuring out how to dispose of anything related to Laplace's Box.

00:23:39.430 --> 00:23:40.830
She's right!

00:23:40.830 --> 00:23:44.520
We should destroy the Unicorn's electronic systems while we have the chance.

00:23:45.130 --> 00:23:46.460
That thing is the "key", right?

00:23:46.460 --> 00:23:50.460
It's not the actual "Box", so if we destroy it, the safety of the Box will—

00:23:55.550 --> 00:24:00.290
Show me the pride of a Federation soldier, Commander Daguza Mackle.

00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:04.520
If you have the nerve, then destroy the key and kill me as well.

00:24:05.150 --> 00:24:10.570
Losing the key and me will undoubtedly deal a blow to Neo Zeon.

00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:15.280
Otherwise, you can keep doing nothing and let them take everything from you.

00:24:15.700 --> 00:24:16.950
There is no time to delay.

00:24:21.250 --> 00:24:22.120
Audrey!

00:24:23.370 --> 00:24:24.960
You can't talk like that.

00:24:25.540 --> 00:24:27.500
You're backing everyone into a corner, including yourself.

00:24:27.500 --> 00:24:28.380
Banagher...

00:24:29.340 --> 00:24:30.170
Let's get out of here.

00:24:30.590 --> 00:24:32.470
This isn't something for you to be involved in!

00:24:34.840 --> 00:24:36.610
I am Mineva Zabi.

00:24:37.140 --> 00:24:38.350
You're Audrey!

00:24:38.350 --> 00:24:41.260
Whether it's your real name or not, to me you're still Audrey Burne!

00:24:41.260 --> 00:24:42.140
Enough!

00:24:42.480 --> 00:24:44.760
This is no time for children to be arguing.

00:24:44.760 --> 00:24:47.710
"Children"? What about Audrey?

00:24:48.150 --> 00:24:50.460
She is a Neo Zeon dignitary.

00:24:50.460 --> 00:24:53.110
But if I'm just a kid, Audrey is too!

00:24:53.530 --> 00:24:56.720
And now you're holding this kid hostage! Is that how adults behave?!

00:24:59.370 --> 00:25:01.620
Time's up. Let's hear your answer.

00:25:09.290 --> 00:25:11.920
Understood. Now we'll destroy your vessel.

00:25:11.920 --> 00:25:13.130
Here it comes!

00:25:13.550 --> 00:25:17.110
Anti-air defenses, ready! Mobile suit corps, prepare to intercept!

00:25:18.550 --> 00:25:19.550
It's just a box.

00:25:20.600 --> 00:25:22.530
Why don't you hand it over to them?!

00:25:24.060 --> 00:25:25.980
We don't even know what it is.

00:25:25.980 --> 00:25:27.540
Why do so many people have to die for it?

00:25:27.980 --> 00:25:29.860
So would you take the responsibility?

00:25:31.860 --> 00:25:36.530
They say whatever is hidden in Laplace's Box could overthrow the Federation.

00:25:36.860 --> 00:25:42.800
If you give that to Neo Zeon, and even more lives are lost...

00:25:42.800 --> 00:25:46.370
Then how do you intend to apologize to the dead and their families.

00:25:48.750 --> 00:25:49.690
Continue.

00:25:51.210 --> 00:25:55.010
Cease fire immediately! Otherwise we will execute Mineva Zabi.

00:25:56.090 --> 00:25:57.490
This is not an empty threat.

00:25:57.800 --> 00:25:59.760
Cease your attacks at once!

00:26:01.430 --> 00:26:05.600
If we take down that red mobile suit, then you won't need Audrey as a hostage, right?

00:26:06.160 --> 00:26:07.180
I'll do it!

00:26:21.840 --> 00:26:23.580
Stand down! Withdraw!!

00:26:23.580 --> 00:26:24.490
Riddhe!

00:26:24.490 --> 00:26:26.350
If it weren't for you we wouldn't be

00:26:31.170 --> 00:26:34.590
trying to play hostage games with a bunch of terrorists!

00:26:48.580 --> 00:26:50.500
Ensign Riddhe, get a grip!

00:26:55.880 --> 00:26:57.110
Commander!

00:27:02.660 --> 00:27:03.530
Commander Norm...

00:27:08.930 --> 00:27:09.890
You bastard!

00:27:15.360 --> 00:27:16.670
What the...?!

00:27:22.180 --> 00:27:22.990
Gundam...

00:27:24.680 --> 00:27:26.370
The Gundam is on catapult one!

00:27:26.370 --> 00:27:28.930
What are you doing? Stop it!

00:27:28.930 --> 00:27:30.640
Gundam pilot, identify yourself!

00:27:30.980 --> 00:27:32.370
You are not cleared for launch.

00:27:32.370 --> 00:27:33.580
Return to the ship immediately!

00:27:34.110 --> 00:27:35.080
You...

00:27:35.770 --> 00:27:38.780
This is a compromise that works for everyone.

00:27:38.780 --> 00:27:41.320
The Unicorn's performance is rock-solid.

00:27:41.320 --> 00:27:45.660
Even a novice pilot with no training can buy us enough time to get out of here.

00:27:45.660 --> 00:27:47.790
You're practically giving away the Box.

00:27:47.790 --> 00:27:51.580
But that's only the key. If the key is broken, the Box will never open

00:27:51.580 --> 00:27:54.380
and the Federation's interests will be protected.

00:27:56.340 --> 00:28:01.070
He'll fight for us and won't quit until the Unicorn is destroyed.

00:28:03.470 --> 00:28:05.160
You can hear me, can't you, Banagher?

00:28:06.240 --> 00:28:08.910
You already know how to initiate the system, don't you?

00:28:12.730 --> 00:28:14.730
Banagher, don't do this!

00:28:15.420 --> 00:28:22.070
That pilot suit has a system that pharmacologically reduces the strain on the body from G resistance.

00:28:22.570 --> 00:28:26.090
Once the NT-D is activated, it'll work automatically.

00:28:26.570 --> 00:28:27.300
NT-D?

00:28:27.300 --> 00:28:30.910
That's the mode in which the Unicorn's limiter is disengaged.

00:28:30.910 --> 00:28:34.310
You've handled it once before. You'll be fine.

00:28:35.500 --> 00:28:36.750
Preparations for launch complete!

00:28:41.840 --> 00:28:42.980
Detaching!

00:29:00.250 --> 00:29:01.280
Found it!

00:29:09.970 --> 00:29:11.120
Amazing...

00:29:20.860 --> 00:29:22.270
It barely grazed him, but...

00:29:27.570 --> 00:29:28.760
Captain!

00:29:34.640 --> 00:29:38.810
I can't believe I fired. I've ruined the Captain's perfect battlefield!

00:29:40.060 --> 00:29:41.670
You made me shoot!

00:29:43.570 --> 00:29:44.440
Gotta keep calm.

00:30:25.690 --> 00:30:28.130
It doesn't matter how powerful they are if they can't hit me!

00:30:39.890 --> 00:30:41.250
You moved for me?

00:30:46.340 --> 00:30:47.400
An I-Field?!

00:31:11.660 --> 00:31:12.530
I did it?

00:31:25.550 --> 00:31:26.610
Audrey...

00:32:23.230 --> 00:32:24.020
I can see now...

00:32:25.860 --> 00:32:27.480
So this is Gundam.

00:32:35.990 --> 00:32:37.970
You're my opponent again, Gundam?

00:32:37.970 --> 00:32:39.220
Withdraw now!

00:32:39.620 --> 00:32:41.660
If you don't withdraw, then Audrey will...

00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:46.670
We'll flank it! Climb!

00:33:06.870 --> 00:33:08.020
Get back!

00:33:08.020 --> 00:33:09.080
Don't charge in too close!

00:33:16.320 --> 00:33:17.110
Behind you!

00:33:18.490 --> 00:33:19.430
The Quad-wing?!

00:33:31.590 --> 00:33:32.550
I'm sorry,

00:33:33.210 --> 00:33:34.130
Audrey...

00:33:45.040 --> 00:33:47.070
Why is that boy inside a Gundam?

00:33:47.070 --> 00:33:49.230
Much appreciated, Lieutenant Marida Cruz.

00:33:54.110 --> 00:33:56.070
I'm sorry, Audrey.

00:34:32.480 --> 00:34:36.990
As a child, I remember seeing a Zabi family speech on TV...

00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:40.410
Sieg Zeon, Sieg Zeon...

00:34:41.620 --> 00:34:43.160
It was a terrifying image.

00:34:44.080 --> 00:34:50.500
Thousands of people were shouting in unison incited by Gihren Zabi, your uncle.

00:34:52.170 --> 00:34:53.790
I guess you, Neo Zeon, still do now.

00:34:54.170 --> 00:34:55.800
"Sieg Zeon..."

00:34:56.300 --> 00:34:57.690
Go ahead and say it for me now.

00:34:58.130 --> 00:34:58.940
Say it!

00:35:03.140 --> 00:35:07.260
Convince me that you're really a Princess of Zeon.

00:35:07.260 --> 00:35:09.170
Otherwise...

00:35:09.170 --> 00:35:14.790
Why did someone like Mineva Zabi slip aboard a Federation ship all by herself?

00:35:15.400 --> 00:35:17.880
The professionals will find that out from you.

00:35:22.120 --> 00:35:24.410
One thing you should remember, though...

00:35:25.990 --> 00:35:28.600
He was calling your name until the very end.

00:35:29.660 --> 00:35:33.170
Not "Mineva Zabi", he kept calling you "Audrey".

00:35:36.710 --> 00:35:38.460
You don't understand anything.

00:35:39.470 --> 00:35:42.680
Who are these "professionals" you mentioned?

00:35:43.180 --> 00:35:45.220
We have official investigators.

00:35:46.600 --> 00:35:49.270
They'll never bring this matter to any judicial authorities.

00:35:49.930 --> 00:35:53.580
Nor will my presence here be made known to the public.

00:35:55.190 --> 00:35:59.570
Full Frontal stubbornly refused to accept that I am actually Mineva Zabi.

00:35:59.570 --> 00:36:00.710
Why do you think that is?

00:36:00.710 --> 00:36:05.530
That was just to negate our hostage tactics.

00:36:05.970 --> 00:36:08.030
Think about it and you'll see.

00:36:08.410 --> 00:36:11.580
How have I managed to keep from being captured for almost ten years?

00:36:12.210 --> 00:36:15.040
And how has Neo Zeon once again been able to have bases in the Earth Sphere

00:36:15.040 --> 00:36:16.940
and build up its armaments?

00:36:17.710 --> 00:36:19.270
You're saying there were backdoor dealings?

00:36:19.960 --> 00:36:23.760
The incident at Industrial 7 will disappear from your news reports.

00:36:24.760 --> 00:36:28.050
It won't be easy for the families and friends of those who died to forgive it.

00:36:28.760 --> 00:36:31.890
But Spacenoids have long been accustomed to these kinds of outrages.

00:36:32.310 --> 00:36:38.230
And the Federation has allowed us to exist as a scapegoat for their anger and frustration.

00:36:39.230 --> 00:36:40.230
At least, until now...

00:36:41.240 --> 00:36:44.300
Laplace's Box has upset the balance?

00:36:44.910 --> 00:36:49.800
The Federation might be taking steps to resolve its relationship with Neo Zeon once and for all.

00:36:51.010 --> 00:36:55.710
That's why the Vist Foundation offered up its precious box.

00:36:57.790 --> 00:36:58.920
Sounds complicated.

00:37:01.260 --> 00:37:03.630
I've always thought of myself as a pilot.

00:37:04.510 --> 00:37:09.660
My job is simply to operate a mobile suit, complete the missions I'm assigned

00:37:10.310 --> 00:37:11.930
and I don't need to think about anything else.

00:37:12.890 --> 00:37:14.480
Even if there's corruption once in a while

00:37:14.480 --> 00:37:18.310
I believed that the Federation had the ability to correct itself.

00:37:20.270 --> 00:37:21.650
Except, that's not true.

00:37:21.650 --> 00:37:24.360
I was just trying not to see it. Not think about it,

00:37:24.360 --> 00:37:26.320
ever since I was with my family.

00:37:27.320 --> 00:37:30.180
Why have you acted alone?

00:37:31.830 --> 00:37:35.120
I too was born into a certain family.

00:37:35.920 --> 00:37:38.690
The family that shouldered the blame for the One Year War.

00:37:40.340 --> 00:37:42.960
I cannot consider myself separate from politics.

00:37:43.460 --> 00:37:46.300
And if the same mistakes are about to be repeated

00:37:46.760 --> 00:37:48.570
I am obligated to prevent it, at the cost of my life.

00:37:48.570 --> 00:37:49.890
It is my responsibility.

00:37:50.810 --> 00:37:53.350
Hey, Riddhe. There's activity around the ship.

00:37:53.350 --> 00:37:54.770
The supply corps is here, I'll bet.

00:37:55.350 --> 00:37:56.480
No one will come here.

00:37:56.890 --> 00:37:58.600
I also stopped the cameras.

00:37:58.900 --> 00:37:59.690
I know.

00:38:01.650 --> 00:38:03.540
You are a person of Zeon.

00:38:04.320 --> 00:38:07.490
Even if you've been secretly collaborating, you're an enemy here.

00:38:07.490 --> 00:38:09.550
You guys killed Commander Norm and the others.

00:38:10.070 --> 00:38:12.430
I simply can't forgive that.

00:38:13.700 --> 00:38:14.680
I understand.

00:38:18.330 --> 00:38:20.400
You said your name is Riddhe Marcenas, correct?

00:38:21.590 --> 00:38:22.480
Yeah.

00:38:22.880 --> 00:38:24.380
Meaning the family you were born into...

00:38:25.840 --> 00:38:27.670
I wish we could've met under different circumstances.

00:38:36.520 --> 00:38:38.020
What I can do...

00:39:11.280 --> 00:39:16.470
I hear this is a replica of a room in the last fortress of the former Principality, A Baoa Qu.

00:39:18.060 --> 00:39:22.350
The Governor General of Palau is an ardent sympathizer of the former Principality of Zeon.

00:39:22.770 --> 00:39:25.270
I must accept a favor like this graciously.

00:39:25.730 --> 00:39:27.360
Even if the decor isn't really my style.

00:39:28.360 --> 00:39:32.160
I suppose that's one necessary trait of a leader.

00:39:33.410 --> 00:39:37.390
Good job Captain, Lieutenant Marida. I'll take it from here.

00:39:38.660 --> 00:39:39.500
Captain...

00:39:39.830 --> 00:39:40.660
I know.

00:39:41.420 --> 00:39:45.100
Princess Mineva being held aboard that ship was unexpected.

00:39:46.500 --> 00:39:50.590
But there will be other chances to rescue her, including political methods.

00:39:50.590 --> 00:39:51.690
We have to deal with it for now.

00:39:51.690 --> 00:39:52.590
Yes.

00:39:58.270 --> 00:39:59.890
Char Aznable...

00:40:00.680 --> 00:40:02.660
What are you doing? Have a seat.

00:40:06.210 --> 00:40:07.770
How're you feeling?

00:40:08.440 --> 00:40:12.700
I hear we went through a lot to get you safely out of that Gundam.

00:40:14.450 --> 00:40:15.530
Well...

00:40:16.830 --> 00:40:20.260
Were you the pilot of that red mobile suit?

00:40:21.710 --> 00:40:26.020
You can't drink tea with a mortal enemy, Banagher Links?

00:40:38.430 --> 00:40:39.470
Good reflexes.

00:40:40.430 --> 00:40:41.720
But a little reckless.

00:40:42.310 --> 00:40:43.640
A temperament befitting a pilot.

00:40:55.070 --> 00:40:56.180
If you don't mind me asking...

00:40:57.030 --> 00:41:00.870
Do you wear that mask to hide some kind of scar?

00:41:02.040 --> 00:41:05.280
Because if not, I'd like you to show me your face.

00:41:05.280 --> 00:41:06.020
You—!

00:41:06.020 --> 00:41:10.550
It's fine, Lieutenant Angelo. Banagher's talking about simple etiquette.

00:41:16.400 --> 00:41:18.680
I only wear it because it's my style.

00:41:19.510 --> 00:41:21.160
Or you could say it's a tool of propaganda.

00:41:21.890 --> 00:41:25.980
Without someone like you to point it out to me, I usually forget I even have it on.

00:41:26.560 --> 00:41:27.670
My apologies.

00:41:32.590 --> 00:41:34.820
I've heard about how you met Princess Mineva.

00:41:36.380 --> 00:41:43.480
But as for how you received that mobile suit, that Unicorn Gundam from the Vist Foundation

00:41:43.480 --> 00:41:45.600
there is much that remains unclear.

00:41:46.210 --> 00:41:49.540
We were supposed to receive that machine.

00:41:50.590 --> 00:41:54.920
So why did Cardeas Vist choose you to be the bearer of Laplace's Box?

00:41:55.550 --> 00:42:01.570
They asked me that while I was being escorted here, and I told them all I know.

00:42:04.430 --> 00:42:07.890
The glory of the Vist Foundation was built on its secret possession of the Box.

00:42:08.770 --> 00:42:12.880
But they decided to break the pact with the Federation government and hand it over to us.

00:42:12.880 --> 00:42:15.570
So their plan couldn't be altered easily.

00:42:16.400 --> 00:42:18.820
Even if the original plan had gone awry

00:42:18.820 --> 00:42:21.620
I can't believe he'd entrust the Box to a random stranger.

00:42:23.080 --> 00:42:24.470
It's more likely

00:42:25.040 --> 00:42:28.310
that you have some relation to the Vist family.

00:42:29.460 --> 00:42:31.440
Am I obligated to respond to that?

00:42:36.610 --> 00:42:38.550
I said stop it, Angelo.

00:42:39.590 --> 00:42:41.450
You'd better realize who you're talking to, punk.

00:42:43.560 --> 00:42:44.680
You're not obligated to respond.

00:42:45.700 --> 00:42:48.770
We simply want information about the Box.

00:42:49.600 --> 00:42:51.270
We're only asking you nicely

00:42:51.270 --> 00:42:53.830
because you're acquainted with Princess Mineva.

00:42:53.830 --> 00:42:55.440
Keep that in mind.

00:42:56.150 --> 00:42:56.940
"Mineva"...

00:42:58.490 --> 00:43:02.660
Audrey is the one who told me Neo Zeon mustn't get their hands on the Box.

00:43:03.030 --> 00:43:05.600
She said it would lead to another great war.

00:43:07.450 --> 00:43:08.710
And after what happened

00:43:09.420 --> 00:43:13.590
to our colony, Industrial 7, anyone would feel the same way.

00:43:14.710 --> 00:43:16.670
She is a Princess of Zeon, right?

00:43:17.420 --> 00:43:21.080
If Audrey is against it, why are all of you—

00:43:21.080 --> 00:43:25.580
Tell me, do you believe in it? In the existence of Laplace's Box?

00:43:26.830 --> 00:43:31.100
Do you believe there's a box no one has ever seen and whose contents are unknown

00:43:31.520 --> 00:43:35.710
but hides the power to completely destroy the Federation government?

00:43:36.440 --> 00:43:39.320
Well, I really don't know.

00:43:40.610 --> 00:43:46.830
But I believe there's such a thing as knowledge which can change the world in an instant.

00:43:47.540 --> 00:43:48.430
Such as?

00:43:51.500 --> 00:43:56.840
For example, like Zeon's first colony drop, or dropping an asteroid to freeze the Earth,

00:43:57.670 --> 00:43:59.460
or in the older eras when nuclear bombs were created,

00:43:59.460 --> 00:44:01.840
or when Minovsky particles were discovered, or mobile suits were invented.

00:44:03.010 --> 00:44:06.640
Even though it seems stable, the world changes little by little.

00:44:07.350 --> 00:44:10.930
If an invention or experiment has that kind of power, and the timing is right...

00:44:12.520 --> 00:44:13.560
You're right about that.

00:44:14.310 --> 00:44:17.150
And if you know your history so well

00:44:17.150 --> 00:44:20.570
you know that space settlement was a policy to exile mass populations, right?

00:44:21.700 --> 00:44:24.490
You probably realize that even when a Side's autonomy is recognized

00:44:24.490 --> 00:44:28.160
the central government retains the right to appoint its leaders.

00:44:28.950 --> 00:44:36.540
Since they can't vote for the central government, the Spacenoids may as well have no suffrage.

00:44:38.770 --> 00:44:40.760
Neo Zeon is not a monolithic society.

00:44:41.380 --> 00:44:45.860
But we all share the desire to change this distorted system.

00:44:46.550 --> 00:44:52.100
In order to break the chains of the Federation and realize Spacenoid autonomy, we need to—

00:44:52.100 --> 00:44:53.830
But it's wrong to resort to terrorism!

00:44:54.690 --> 00:44:58.270
Whatever your reasons, you can't arbitrarily take lives!

00:44:58.770 --> 00:45:00.500
No one has that right!

00:45:01.740 --> 00:45:03.610
That goes for you too!

00:45:09.280 --> 00:45:13.000
If force is always wrong, you're just as guilty for using the Gundam!

00:45:13.410 --> 00:45:16.500
You killed one of our valued men out there!

00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:18.540
I... what...?

00:45:19.190 --> 00:45:23.360
It may have been a stray shot, but you're still the one who shot him down!

00:45:24.760 --> 00:45:27.140
I don't think that realization has hit Banagher yet.

00:45:27.760 --> 00:45:29.850
He probably acted out of desperation.

00:45:32.810 --> 00:45:35.040
Ensign Sergi was unlucky.

00:45:35.390 --> 00:45:37.600
I... killed someone.

00:45:38.270 --> 00:45:39.400
Call for Zinnerman.

00:45:40.820 --> 00:45:43.840
You have a lot to learn yet.

00:45:45.070 --> 00:45:46.650
I want you to understand who we are.

00:45:47.570 --> 00:45:52.010
And I hope we can eventually work together.

00:46:00.960 --> 00:46:04.590
Are you...are you really Char Aznable?

00:46:07.840 --> 00:46:11.350
As I am now, I consider myself a vessel.

00:46:12.100 --> 00:46:18.750
A vessel for the hopes of those abandoned in space, and for the heirs of Zeon's ideals.

00:46:20.920 --> 00:46:24.820
And if that's what they want, I will be Char Aznable.

00:46:25.900 --> 00:46:27.920
That's why I wear this mask.

00:46:46.840 --> 00:46:47.920
Palau.

00:46:48.800 --> 00:46:52.470
It's a civilian mining asteroid belonging to Side 6.

00:46:52.930 --> 00:46:58.410
Our intelligence agency has concluded that the RX-0 was taken here.

00:46:58.410 --> 00:47:03.170
The Nahel Argama is supposed to break into that fortress alone? Not possible.

00:47:03.170 --> 00:47:05.900
This operation is under ECOAS jurisdiction.

00:47:05.900 --> 00:47:08.440
Reinforcements have already arrived for that purpose.

00:47:08.820 --> 00:47:14.430
It's unprecedented for two elite ECOAS teams to join forces like this...

00:47:14.430 --> 00:47:16.430
What are our odds?

00:47:17.040 --> 00:47:21.830
If we're supposed to recapture the RX-0, seizing control of one area isn't going to cut it.

00:47:21.830 --> 00:47:22.880
Amazing! It's Hyaku Shiki!

00:47:22.880 --> 00:47:27.960
We'll need to sabotage a wide area in order to prevent enemy pursuit.

00:47:28.880 --> 00:47:30.900
Do you agree with this plan, Captain?

00:47:32.050 --> 00:47:38.180
If we're going to attack a stronghold, shouldn't we assemble all of Londo Bell's forces?

00:47:38.680 --> 00:47:42.750
It seems like Headquarters is asking us to go on a suicide mission.

00:47:42.750 --> 00:47:47.570
That's why we're sending out two expensive teams of special forces.

00:47:47.900 --> 00:47:50.530
That's the best we can manage for a covert operation.

00:47:50.900 --> 00:47:52.470
We're not asking you!

00:47:52.470 --> 00:47:56.330
The RX-0 is lost now because of what you did!

00:47:57.950 --> 00:48:00.870
The situation developed in an unexpected way but...

00:48:00.870 --> 00:48:02.750
If it hadn't been for that, the ship would have been destroye—

00:48:06.090 --> 00:48:07.090
I'll be right back.

00:48:12.900 --> 00:48:14.450
Damn it!

00:48:14.450 --> 00:48:16.430
You call those reinforcements?!

00:48:16.890 --> 00:48:19.370
You call this a covert operation?!

00:48:19.770 --> 00:48:23.870
Spouting desperate excuses to make up for his own failure!

00:48:24.620 --> 00:48:27.000
Damn you!

00:48:35.950 --> 00:48:39.930
We've heard about our orders from Headquarters. What do you intend to do?

00:48:39.930 --> 00:48:41.330
We have no choice but to go.

00:48:41.960 --> 00:48:45.690
Because it's related to the Box which is supposed to determine the fate of the world.

00:48:45.690 --> 00:48:48.440
I have no objection to our orders either...

00:48:49.440 --> 00:48:53.970
But we consider it a hostage rescue mission.

00:48:55.800 --> 00:48:59.240
We owe it to him. And I know of a way.

00:48:59.870 --> 00:49:04.140
This ship is equipped with a hyper mega particle gun, isn't it?

00:49:08.400 --> 00:49:09.980
The Federation's movement has me concerned.

00:49:11.990 --> 00:49:15.360
Depending on the situation, we might need to abandon this place.

00:49:17.240 --> 00:49:19.030
You think the Federation is going to attack?

00:49:20.950 --> 00:49:23.450
How's the analysis of the Unicorn Gundam going?

00:49:40.600 --> 00:49:42.310
Hey, are you from the Federation?

00:49:42.640 --> 00:49:44.020
Tikva, be quiet and eat.

00:49:45.190 --> 00:49:47.440
These guys forced me to come here.

00:49:50.070 --> 00:49:51.520
Sit still and eat properly, young lady.

00:49:52.110 --> 00:49:52.980
You're a prisoner?

00:49:52.980 --> 00:49:54.080
Something like that.

00:49:54.080 --> 00:49:56.400
Oh, then you're lucky to be our prisoner!

00:49:56.860 --> 00:50:00.240
If you were a Federation prisoner, they wouldn't give you anything to eat.

00:50:00.870 --> 00:50:02.120
You'd be tortured!

00:50:02.540 --> 00:50:04.390
Tikva, don't talk while you're eating.

00:50:05.080 --> 00:50:06.770
The Federation doesn't do things like that.

00:50:07.080 --> 00:50:09.080
Yeah, they do. My dad says so.

00:50:09.380 --> 00:50:13.130
He was a prisoner on Earth, and the Captain helped him in the camp.

00:50:14.720 --> 00:50:18.720
Well, there are many people whose friends and family were killed by Zeon.

00:50:21.450 --> 00:50:24.430
Yeah, same goes for us obviously. That's war.

00:50:25.060 --> 00:50:27.270
But Zeon was fighting for the Spacenoids.

00:50:27.890 --> 00:50:29.600
And you're a Spacenoid, aren't you?

00:50:29.940 --> 00:50:31.880
How come you're on the Federation's side?

00:50:31.880 --> 00:50:34.480
That's enough. You'll make your dad angry.

00:50:35.110 --> 00:50:37.240
No war is ever justified.

00:50:39.070 --> 00:50:40.910
Even if what you're saying is "right"

00:50:40.910 --> 00:50:45.160
that doesn't change the fact that Zeon dropped an entire colony and killed lots of people.

00:50:46.580 --> 00:50:51.190
The people who were killed never had a chance to think about what was "right" or not.

00:50:51.920 --> 00:50:54.090
They didn't know anything about it, and then one day, suddenly...

00:50:54.090 --> 00:50:55.460
It just wasn't fair.

00:50:56.190 --> 00:50:58.130
That's right. Not fair at all.

00:50:59.970 --> 00:51:01.090
There was nothing else I could do.

00:51:01.510 --> 00:51:02.930
I never intended to kill, but...

00:51:03.930 --> 00:51:05.260
I was about to be killed.

00:51:07.480 --> 00:51:09.750
I am not a murderer.

00:51:13.860 --> 00:51:14.860
Come with me.

00:51:29.920 --> 00:51:31.790
What you're saying is not wrong.

00:51:33.090 --> 00:51:35.590
There is no truly justifiable war, but...

00:51:36.300 --> 00:51:38.550
...justice does not always save lives.

00:51:48.180 --> 00:51:52.230
This was built back when Palau was still in the asteroid belt.

00:51:54.190 --> 00:51:56.570
When you think about the earliest space pioneers

00:51:56.570 --> 00:52:02.240
they were mostly beggars and political criminals, without any other way to live.

00:52:03.320 --> 00:52:05.370
I hear that when the Universal Century began

00:52:05.370 --> 00:52:09.330
the Prime Minister stated in his speech that we were "bringing an end to the Era of God", but

00:52:10.910 --> 00:52:16.250
the people living in the asteroid belt, where the sun is indistinguishable from any other stars,

00:52:16.250 --> 00:52:18.590
probably needed a light to guide them.

00:52:20.220 --> 00:52:21.170
A light...

00:52:21.720 --> 00:52:23.970
No one can live without light.

00:52:24.430 --> 00:52:29.560
But the people abandoned in space eventually found a light to replace God.

00:52:31.140 --> 00:52:34.080
A new light called Zeon.

00:52:35.860 --> 00:52:38.190
It was what they needed.

00:52:39.340 --> 00:52:43.610
So that they could resist despair and keep living in this cruel world.

00:52:44.740 --> 00:52:48.950
Something that made them think there was room in this world for improvement.

00:52:50.450 --> 00:52:52.410
Some might say you can live without that.

00:52:53.210 --> 00:52:56.380
Or that it's stupid to cling to something so intangible.

00:52:56.380 --> 00:52:59.190
If they're sure about that

00:52:59.190 --> 00:53:05.220
those people must be true optimists or completely detached from reality.

00:53:11.520 --> 00:53:13.580
Humanity alone possesses a God.

00:53:15.520 --> 00:53:17.100
Someone once told me that.

00:53:17.730 --> 00:53:22.320
The power to transcend the now, the inner God called "possibility".

00:53:23.200 --> 00:53:24.530
He must have been a romantic.

00:53:25.470 --> 00:53:29.220
A person can't say that without faith in humanity and the world.

00:53:30.080 --> 00:53:31.790
Sounds like a nice person.

00:53:35.100 --> 00:53:36.480
Ensign Sergi...

00:53:38.000 --> 00:53:40.340
Don't worry about the one you shot down.

00:53:41.800 --> 00:53:46.430
When anyone goes into battle in a mobile suit, they become a combat unit called a pilot.

00:53:46.930 --> 00:53:48.450
There's no need for regrets.

00:53:49.890 --> 00:53:50.760
But...

00:53:51.310 --> 00:53:55.640
Keep in mind that you are already a part of the situation.

00:53:58.690 --> 00:54:02.420
And as for taking action to help Princess Mineva, I'm grateful to you.

00:54:07.280 --> 00:54:08.360
Do you—

00:54:08.360 --> 00:54:09.380
Umm...

00:54:11.950 --> 00:54:12.850
Marida.

00:54:13.660 --> 00:54:16.770
Do you pilot a mobile suit too, Ms. Marida?

00:54:18.080 --> 00:54:19.940
When we're short on manpower, yes.

00:54:26.800 --> 00:54:27.610
Time to eat.

00:54:28.390 --> 00:54:30.140
Better finish before the ship starts combat operations.

00:54:37.690 --> 00:54:38.580
It's you...

00:54:44.150 --> 00:54:44.920
Come with me.

00:54:59.330 --> 00:55:00.560
We're going to Earth.

00:55:14.700 --> 00:55:16.290
Sorry man.

00:55:19.190 --> 00:55:20.190
Wait!

00:55:25.170 --> 00:55:26.380
What's wrong?

00:55:26.380 --> 00:55:27.530
Nothing...

00:55:43.880 --> 00:55:46.630
14th space gate... 3rd port...

00:55:47.130 --> 00:55:48.330
By 00:00:00 Zulu...

00:55:48.330 --> 00:55:49.800
Stay on schedule...

00:55:50.130 --> 00:55:51.400
The safety of your life...

00:55:52.430 --> 00:55:53.390
Your life!

00:56:02.270 --> 00:56:03.330
This time...

00:56:04.400 --> 00:56:05.940
this place is going to be a battlefield?

